  "bloques": [
    {
      "tipo": "explicacion",
      "titulo": {
        "en": "Online in Spanish"
      },
      "texto": {
        "en": "Many everyday verbs for using devices are regular in the present: **descargar**, **subir**, **enviar**, **reenviar**, **borrar**, **guardar**, **instalar**, **actualizar**, **iniciar sesión**. **Colgar** (**cuelgo**) has an *o → ue* stem change and means to post something online as well as to hang up.\n\nLoanwords are adapted to Spanish spelling and pronunciation: **el/la wifi**, **el clic**, **chatear**, **un blog**.\n\nIn Spain people usually say **el móvil** and **el ordenador**; across Latin America **el celular** and **la computadora** (or **el computador**) are the usual terms.\n\nTo read an email address aloud: **@** is **arroba**, a dot is **punto**, **-** is **guion**, and **_** is **guion bajo**. So *ana.ruiz@correo.es* is read *ana punto ruiz arroba correo punto es*."
      }
    },
